{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "zone-dusk",
  "category": "environment",
  "status": "provisional",
  "comment": "THE DUSK VERGE: the dusk of the reference image — a sky that goes from violet to crimson, thin crooked trees that stand on their own roots and hold a sphere of red light, a pink mist over the ground and the first pools of lava. What makes the zone that zone: the three seamless strips of its backdrop, tall enough for the camera of every room of it; the ground its rooms are built of; the pieces that stand, lie and hang in them; the spikes of its ditches; the lava, its fall and its embers; and the light in its colour. Painted by the generator in tools/art (npm run art:build), not by a person: provisional until an artist reviews or replaces it.",
